<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  iOS entitlements for the AUv3 extension: deliberately EMPTY.

	  Two keys used to live here and both were wrong:
	  - com.apple.security.app-sandbox is a macOS entitlement, copied over with
	    the file. Meaningless on iOS, and a device install may reject it.
	  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit does nothing on iOS (no JIT write
	    protection API, interpreter compiled in instead - see
	    src/compat/exec_mem.h and the SMU2000_SH2_JIT switch).

	  Deliberately no application-groups either. Working without a paid account
	  means free provisioning, which does not support App Groups, so the
	  extension cannot reach the app's files through a shared container. The
	  ROMs are therefore baked into the extension bundle instead
	  (make ios-auv3 IOS_ROMS=roms), which the engine finds beside the binary
	  (candidate 3b in src/vst3/engine.cpp).

	  "import ROMs" from inside the app can come later; it would write into the
	  bundle-adjacent directory or, once there is a paid account, into a group
	  container.

	  If background audio is ever needed (playing while another app is front),
	  that is UIBackgroundModes=audio in the *app's* Info.plist, not an
	  entitlement here.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
